1. Proprietary QCP binary tools
==============================

The QCP binary tools distributed in linux-binary/, win-binary/,
mac-x86-64-binary/, and mac-arm64-binary/, and equivalent QCP binary tool
distributions, are proprietary, closed-source software (the "Binary Software").
The Binary Software is not open source and is not covered by the MIT License
in Section 2. Distribution of the Binary Software does not grant access to,
or rights in, its source code.

Universities and research institutes in China may use the current version
and all historical versions of the Binary Software free of charge for
non-commercial educational and research purposes.

Any individual or organization wishing to use the Binary Software for
commercial purposes must pay the applicable license fee and obtain prior
authorization from the copyright holders before such use. This requirement
also applies to commercial use by universities and research institutes.
For commercial licensing, contact: caoqinxiang@sjtu.edu.cn

All rights in the Binary Software not expressly granted above or in a separate
license agreement are reserved. These terms do not revoke rights already
granted under a license applicable to a previously received copy.

THE BINARY SOFTWARE IS PROVIDED "AS IS", WITHOUT WARRANTY OF ANY KIND, EXPRESS
OR IMPLIED, INCLUDING BUT NOT LIMITED TO THE WARRANTIES OF MERCHANTABILITY,
